      "id": "sol.amc-8-2002-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Note that the \\(0\\) digit can either be the tens or the units digit. This gives us \\(2\\) options for this.\n\nThere are \\(9\\) options for each of the other digits for a total of \\[ 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 9 = 162 \\] numbers.\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
